      "source_text": "关系式（6.17）或（6.18）叫做**薄透镜公式**. 量 $d$，$f$ 和 $F$ 可以是正值，也可以是负值. 我们不加证明地指出，在应用透镜公式时，需要根据以下规则在各项前面标上符号. 如果透镜是会聚透镜，那么它的焦点是实焦点，并且项 $\\frac{1}{|F|}$ 前面的符号为“正”. 如果是发散透镜，$F<0$，并且公式（6.17）右边将是负值 $-\\frac{1}{|F|}$. 如果像是实像，项 $\\frac{1}{|f|}$ 的符号为“正”，如是虚像则符号为“负”. 最后，在实发光点的情况下，项 $\\frac{1}{|d|}$ 前的符号为“正”，如果发光点是虚的（即射到透镜上的会聚光束延长线交于一点），则项 $\\frac{1}{|d|}$ 前的符号为“负”.",
      "candidate_text": "Relations (6.17) and (6.18) are called the **thin-lens formula**; $d$, $f$, and $F$ are signed quantities.\nWe use the convention that real objects, real images, and real focal lengths are positive. The formula also applies to virtual objects, virtual images, and diverging lenses; the sign convention is stated here without a further proof.\nA converging lens has a real focus, so the $\\frac{1}{|F|}$ term has a positive sign.\nFor a diverging lens, $F<0$, and the right-hand side is $-\\frac{1}{|F|}$.\nThe $\\frac{1}{|f|}$ term is positive for a real image and negative for a virtual image.\nThe $\\frac{1}{|d|}$ term is positive for a real luminous object; the $\\frac{1}{|d|}$ term is negative for a virtual object.\nA virtual object is the point that incoming converging rays would reach if continued in their incident directions without being changed by the lens. It is not an actual light source at that position.",
